title: Moving a member out of the folder
pid: 1d9fb1de-fa4c-4980-8262-6de934948e6c
body: |2-
  A save never reads a node's content from a headline the view drew
  without that content. A child drawn in a member's folder of what you
  keep elsewhere, or of what your note hides in it, is drawn
  write-protected, folded, without its own content; moved out of the
  folder to stand under the member (to unhide it), it stays
  write-protected, and keeps its content as on disk, until you ask for
  its editable view there ('C-c s e'), which draws that content.

  A member as such is drawn editable, but shows its content only in
  part, so its headline carries =contentInPart=. Moved out of the forks
  folder, into your note's content or anywhere else, it takes the atom
  with it: the save reads its title and body, and nothing under it as
  its content, which stays as on disk; the redrawn view draws that
  content whole, without the atom, and you edit it there. A headline
  typed under it in that same save joins no list, and the save warns of
  the orphan. Its folders of what you keep elsewhere and of what your
  note hides in it belong under a member only, so a save that moves them
  out with it is refused ('tests/moved_headlines_whose_content_was_not_drawn.rs').
